WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.850
"Website for Shikada Dagashi"
"Manager's Blog"
"Dagashi Stories" "Dagashi and toys"
 "Order for delivery" "Contact us" "Location"

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.910
This is my first time ordering.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.560
"Order Form"
"Monjiro Squid 100-pack"
"2,500 yen" "Submit Order"

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:11.990
A dear friend of mine loves dagashi
and wants to eat them every day.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.790
However, my friend will be hospitalized for some time

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.900
and cannot go to the store to buy them.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.120
Then I found out that Shikada Dagashi
has started a delivery service.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.500
That is why I've decided to contact you.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.360
Thank you very much.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
I can't wait to see the big
smile on my friend's face!

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.380
We've received our first order.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.870
At any rate, this person cares
about her friend very--

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:34.510
Hm?

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.510
Manager...

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.180
What a nice person...

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.480
Y-You're crying!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:49.940
My honey!

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.070
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling,
when I take a bite

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.950
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling flows into me

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:03.870
The crackling sparkle is giving me a sugar rush

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:09.210
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.420
A scent drifts into the air...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.590
Could it be you?

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:21.760
With those footsteps that sound like
a colorful and full candy box shaking

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:31.650
I feel like I can reach that cotton
candy in the sky, but it's no good

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:37.860
Don't melt away! Don't disappear!
I want to tell you my feelings!

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.610
You're hungry?

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.160
My honey!

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.820
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.580
The first bite was full of mystery

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.210
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.960
The second bite got me hopelessly addicted

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.460
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:58.300
The more I chew, the deeper the flavor

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.930
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:05.810
Before I knew it, I was
completely crazy about you

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.810
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.950
"Municipal General Hospital"

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.560
Let's see... Yes, this is the right hospital.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.950
But are you really sure about this?

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.950
Sure about what?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.040
That person who wrote that order email
didn't even tell us their name, right?

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.130
It could be a prank.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:38.260
I'm okay with that. If it was a prank,
then that just means there isn't a patient

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.050
who can't go to a dagashi shop.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.890
I guess you're right.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.560
Well... it's this room.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.520
Might as well go in and see.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.350
We're coming in.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.360
Hello! We're from Shikada Daga--

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.280
Oh, hey! Kokonotsu!

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.950
What took you so long?!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.990
Dad?!

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:04.740
Wait! What's with that cast?!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.660
You just broke your little toe, didn't you?!

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.490
Now, hand them over!

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.210
Where are the dagashi?
Give them to me! Dagashi!

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.590
I just got here. You've got a lot of nerve.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.210
Give them to me already. Hey.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.010
What's with that annoying attitude?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.680
Oh? Who's she?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.590
Oh, yeah.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.180
Remember? I mentioned the part-timer
on the phone the other day. It's her.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.050
I'm Hajime Owari. Thank you for hiring me!

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.930
Nice to meet you!

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.020
Kokonotsu...

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.940
Hm?

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.230
Here I thought you hiring a part-timer
was you showing initiative,

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.150
but now, it's clear you were being naughty!

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:40.940
Huh?!

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.410
You like girls who leave their
guard down, don't you...?

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.570
Stop it!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.740
But I'm right, aren't I?!
Kokonotsu, you naughty boy, you!

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:51.580
Argh! Fine, you'll be happy if
I give this to you, right?!

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.210
Here!

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:57.090
"Monjiro Squid"

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:57.340
Whoa! A hundred pack of Monjiro Squid!
You knew what I wanted, huh?!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.920
What do you mean I knew?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.550
I can enjoy them thoroughly one by one.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.840
This is just perfect for a hospital stay.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.850
You can keep chewing on it to enjoy its
strong flavor as long as you want, too.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.350
Yep! It goes well with beer, too.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.650
Do you know why
Monjiro Squid is sold skewered?

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.190
What? Isn't it because
it's easy to eat that way?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.110
Well, that too, but...

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.740
...in a samurai drama that
aired a long time ago,

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.530
this guy had a long bamboo skewer
in his mouth and it was so cool.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.580
So it became a boom.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.710
"That's got nothing to do with me"

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.500
They're using skewers because it's cool?

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.580
Yeah. Don't I look cool?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.830
Coo--?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:38.790
Excuse me.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.800
Do they use real squid?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.380
Yes. Using real flying squids
is one of its selling points.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.470
So it's more like a side dish that goes
well with alcohol rather than dagashi.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.970
"Monjiro Squid"

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.600
I see...

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.980
Well then, we're going home now,
but next time just call in your order, okay?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.940
"Just call in"?

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.020
"Order"?

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.730
You owe me 2,500 yen,
which includes the delivery fee.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.730
What?! I have to pay?!

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.740
Of course you do! This is a delivery service!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.740
"Delivery service"?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.740
This isn't a gift?
Wait, we have a delivery service?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:17.080
Oh come on! You found out about it and
decided to send us that email, right?!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.750
I feel stupid for getting kinda moved by it...

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.760
An email? What're you talking about?

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.130
Huh?! You wanted some Monjiro
Squid and thought it would be fun

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.300
to play a prank too, didn't you?!

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.260
Hey, hey, calm down. I really don't
know what you're talking about.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.170
Then who sent...

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.520
...that email?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.060
Well... it is a good idea, though...

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:38.770
What?

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.310
Delivery service.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.940
Now Shikada Dagashi's future is secured.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:45.610
What do you mean?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:51.540
You renovated the shop. You hired
Hajime and started a delivery service.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:56.620
It means that you finally decided
to take over the shop, right?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:57.830
What?!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.380
So you flat-out gave up on
becoming a manga author, huh?

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.630
W-Wait!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.630
No! It's not like that!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:07.380
Then you're still drawing manga?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.230
I am! I am drawing manga!

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.350
Of course I am!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.720
Oh...

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:20.060
Manga...

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.310
Manager.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.400
Ah, yes.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.860
About what you guys were talking about...

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:26.650
What? Oh, that's... um...

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.910
I thought Monjiro Squid must
be super good with beer.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:32.690
Huh?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.480
Is it okay to stop by the convenience store?

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.920
I haven't been drawing at all...

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.090
How long has it been since
I started working on this?!

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.420
What have I been doing?!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.260
I got caught up in all the
stuff going on every day!

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.430
Didn't I want to become a manga author?!

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.440
How exactly... do you become a manga author?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.260
What?! Hey! H-Hajime?!

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:11.700
Manager...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.060
You reek of alcohol!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.950
About what your dad said earlier...

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:19.710
Are you...

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:24.290
...looking at me like that?

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.380
N-No, I'm not!

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.960
As a matter of fact, I have Hotaru...!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.430
Is it possible... that that order email was...

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.350
..from Hota--

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.230
What? What're you talking about?

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.020
Why are you drunk?

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.020
You're sneaky...

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.900
Thank you very much!

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.490
Hm? It's not safe to walk
while reading, Kokonotsu.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.240
Here it is!

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.000
"On-site Manga Review Event!"

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:01.000
They're holding an on-site manga
review event in each region!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.580
An editor is coming to a town
that's not too far from here.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.000
Let's see... It'll be on Sunday.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.420
What day is it today, Yutaka?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.050
It's Friday.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.090
Can't you wait to read it until you get home?

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.970
The time limit is the day after tomorrow!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.720
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"
"Review event!!"

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:22.230
I'll use today and tomorrow
to finish up the manuscript...

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.400
...and go to the manga review event on Sunday!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.230
"Saturday, December 14"

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.650
This required number of pages... Two days...

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.190
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"
"Review event!!"

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.990
...should be enough to finish it.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.790
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.500
"Saturday, December 14"

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.940
This is really bad...

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:51.670
It's taking longer than I expected!

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:59.510
"Saturday, December 14"

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.510
I thought I could finish it quicker.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.480
There's no way I'll finish on time.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.370
Why didn't I work on it
little-by-little every day?

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.070
This won't work... I'll give up this time and...

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.780
Manager?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.210
Your friends are here.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:24.540
Oh?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.960
Manager... Is that... mang--

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.040
I-I-It's nothing!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.800
This is like a pastime!

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.760
And you should've knocked!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.330
I did.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:37.800
Oh?

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.680
Hm?

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.310
"The day after tomorrow"
"Sunday"
"Review event!!"

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.310
Sunday... Review event...

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.850
Are you going to submit your manga?

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:49.190
Err... I was... going to, but...

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.810
Seriously?!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.980
Manager! Are you really
going to be a manga author?!

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.700
Wow! Why didn't you tell me?!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.490
Good luck with the review event!
I'm rooting for you!

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.210
Um, I appreciate it...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.660
...but there's no way I can finish it.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:08.930
So I thought I might just give up this time.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.870
Don't worry!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.510
Let's finish it by tomorrow morning!

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.340
B-But...

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.970
I'll help you! Let's ask your friends, too!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.390
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.390
I heard what's going on.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.980
Coconuts, I'd love to help
out if you're okay with it!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:33.070
That sounds fun! Count me in, too.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.360
Saya... To...!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.450
That being said, I can only
make coffee for you, though.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:43.200
Then... You can count on me to
play video games next to you

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:44.240
and keep you posted on my progress!

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.040
Guys...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.330
Then I'll work on the
background and other stuff.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.210
On that summer day,
we ate popsicles under the sun

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.500
Um... Is it possible that you used to...

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:54.460
I still have the winning stick you gave me

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.210
I'm a part-timer at Shikada Dagashi.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.460
'cause I'm worried that if I take it to the shop

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.760
even the memory will melt away like a popsicle

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:00.550
It's my job to help my
boss out if he's in trouble.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.930
I'm such a fool to think that way, aren't I?

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:04.050
As the seasons pass, you get even taller

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.000
Okay!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.060
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.290
--All right! I'll go for it!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.220
The dream that was vague
has gotten a bit clearer

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.430
--Let's see, I need a desk.
--All right! I'll go for it!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:10.140
"Shikada Dagashi"
"Monjiro Squid, Manga Manuscript, and..."

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.180
--Let's see, I need a desk.
--I'll use your kitchen, okay?

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:08.890
--Hm? It doesn't turn on!
--I'll use your kitchen, okay?

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.890
When I felt kind of worried and held you tight

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:13.690
you, with your eyes as sweet
as honey, smiled at me

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.860
Festivals, fireworks, that hot summer

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.030
Christmas, Valentine's, the freezing winter

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:25.080
Let's spend the next season together, too

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.370
"It's a promise, okay?"

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:32.460
Adolescence? Who cares about it?
I don't care about forever, either

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:39.260
Beyond the seasons gone by lies the future

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:45.260
I wonder if this pain will go away someday

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:55.400
That's what I was thinking as we ate the same
candy under the same sky on our way home

00:11:55.400 --> 00:12:02.030
I'm strange, aren't I? To feel
like it's a little bittersweet

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time:
'Homerun Bar Winning Stick, Snow, and...'"

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.870
Next time. "Homerun Bar Winning Stick, Snow, and..."

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:16.270
Hm? What? It can't be...! Wh-What?!
